# 3-Color Map Problem

# You have a simple map with four interconnected regions (A, B, C, D). You want
# to color the map using 3 colors (1, 2, or 3) so that no two adjacent regions
# share the same color.

# A is adjacent to B, C, and D.
# B is adjacent to C.
# C is adjacent to D.

# Assign colors 1, 2, or 3 to each region
LET a super 1 3
LET b super 1 3
LET c super 1 3
LET d super 1 3

# Constraints: Adjacent regions cannot have equal colors
CHK not eq a b
CHK not eq a c
CHK not eq a d
CHK not eq b c
CHK not eq c d

# Observe a valid coloring universe
OBS a
OBS b
OBS c
OBS d